  <details>
    <summary>What materials are commonly used for flat roofs in Florida?</summary>
    <p>In Florida, flat roofs commonly use materials like modified bitumen, TPO (Thermoplastic Olefin), and EPDM (Ethylene Propylene Diene Monomer) due to their durability and performance in hot, wet climates.</p>
  </details>
